 "notes": "height.bin (1024×569) = area-average of the 3DEP 1/3″ DEM over each cell (mercator node grid). Sea: 3DEP stores 0 offshore → cells with 3DEP ≤ 0 keep the old Terrarium bathymetry clamped to ≤ −1 m (so the coastline is the 3DEP one; a few sea-level ponds in Hilo also become ≤ 0). normal.png 4096×2278 (16.1 m/px) from the 1/3″ DEM at 8 m (2× supersampled), water = (0,1,0). sat.jpg 8192×4556 (8.06 m/px): 47 NAIP quads from Planetary Computer (read at 4.8 m overview) + 18 quads (Hilo side, acquired Dec 2022/Jan 2023) exported per quad from the NAIP2021_Hawaii ImageServer at 4.3 m, each quad cloud(+shadow)-masked, colour-matched per quad to the old EOX mosaic (10/50/90 % percentiles per channel on 32 m blocks) plus a 700 m local residual field, quads feathered 48 px, everything not covered (NAIP no-data north of Hilo, cloudy NAIP quads mostly in the SE strip and two patches near the Saddle, open sea) falls back to the old EOX image with a 160 px feather — those fallback patches still contain the EOX clouds (≈25 % of land is not at full NAIP weight). Known limitation: faint haze/seamline steps between some Hilo-side quads (vog in the Dec 2022 flights). The NAIP pixels cover the whole 1935 flow path from the vent to the 1935 flow front; no 2022 lava is visible (pre-eruption quads there).",
